<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d11" for="edge" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d10" for="edge" attr.name="seq" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d9" for="edge" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d8" for="edge" attr.name="flow_id" attr.type="long" />
  <key id="d7" for="node" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d6" for="node" attr.name="service" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="graph" attr.name="graph_usable" attr.type="boolean" />
  <key id="d3" for="graph" attr.name="categories" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d2" for="graph" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="graph" attr.name="link" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="0">
      <data key="d5">Developer</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d7">Commits code changes, build definitions and CloudFormation templates to the repository; can modify build and infrastructure on demand by going back to the first stage.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1">
      <data key="d5">CodePipeline</data>
      <data key="d6">CodePipeline</data>
      <data key="d7">Orchestrates the pipeline stages: source (CodeCommit), build (CodeBuild) and deploy (CloudFormation). Supports parallel deploy stages for up to 100 customers.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2">
      <data key="d5">CodeCommit</data>
      <data key="d6">CodeCommit</data>
      <data key="d7">AWS repository where developers commit code; also holds the CloudFormation templates that define the entire application infrastructure and the build configuration.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3">
      <data key="d5">CodeBuild</data>
      <data key="d6">CodeBuild</data>
      <data key="d7">Build stage; spins up a container and is paid only for the build duration. Build behaviour is controlled by the developer via the repository. Outputs a container image on a successful build.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="4">
      <data key="d5">Registry (ECR)</data>
      <data key="d6">ECR</data>
      <data key="d7">Amazon ECR registry holding the application container image, ready to be deployed.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5">
      <data key="d5">CloudFormation</data>
      <data key="d6">CloudFormation</data>
      <data key="d7">Third (deploy) stage. Chosen over CodeDeploy, the ECS task definition deployer and Lambda because it deploys the application plus the underlying infrastructure. A single template is the baseline for all production environments; per-customer configuration supplies unique items (VPC name, ECS cluster). Three steps: 1) Change set, 2) Approve (by someone with the proper roles and permissions), 3) Execute. Up to 100 parallel stages for 100 customer VPCs.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6">
      <data key="d5">VPC</data>
      <data key="d6">VPC</data>
      <data key="d7">Per-customer VPC hosting the deployed production product; each customer is deployed to a different VPC (e.g. 100 VPCs). Developer environments are separated from production and client QA environments.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7">
      <data key="d5">ECS</data>
      <data key="d6">ECS</data>
      <data key="d7">Elastic Container Service task definition deployed by CloudFormation; runs the application image.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="8">
      <data key="d5">IAM</data>
      <data key="d6">IAM</data>
      <data key="d7">IAM roles and permissions deployed by CloudFormation as part of the application infrastructure.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="9">
      <data key="d5">ALB</data>
      <data key="d6">ALB</data>
      <data key="d7">Application Load Balancer deployed by CloudFormation as part of the application infrastructure.</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="0" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Developer commits code changes to the CodeCommit repository.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">CodePipeline picks up the commit in the source stage.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="5" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Once the build is done and the image is in the registry, the CloudFormation deploy stage is kicked off (change set, approve, execute); up to 100 parallel stages.</data>
      <data key="d10">4</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">The pipeline moves the commit to the next stage, CodeBuild.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">After a successful build, CodeBuild outputs the application container image to the ECR registry.</data>
      <data key="d10">3</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="6" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation executes the change set and deploys infrastructure and application into the customer VPC (up to 100 different VPCs with the same changes).</data>
      <data key="d10">5</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="7" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Deploys the Elastic Container Service task definition.</data>
      <data key="d10">6</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="8" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Deploys the IAM role and permissions.</data>
      <data key="d10">6'</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="9" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Deploys the application load balancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">6''</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <data key="d0">Aetion: Streamlined CI/CD for Application and Infrastructure Deployment with CodePipeline and CloudFormation</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6YkguepAQuQ</data>
    <data key="d2">Healthcare analytics company pipeline that takes a developer commit through CodeCommit, CodeBuild, ECR and a CloudFormation deploy stage (change set, approve, execute) to deploy application and infrastructure (ECS task definition, IAM role, ALB) into per-customer VPCs, with up to 100 parallel CloudFormation stages.</data>
    <data key="d3">DevOps, CI/CD, Containers, Infrastructure as Code, Healthcare</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
</graphml>
